  "name": "24 HR URINARY UREA",
  "code": "1001",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>A 24-hour urinary urea test measures the amount of urea nitrogen excreted in the urine over a full day. It is primarily used to assess protein metabolism, dietary protein intake, and kidney function.</p>\n<p>Low urea levels may indicate:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&bull; Low protein intake or malnutrition<br>&nbsp;&bull; Kidney problems with reduced urea excretion<br>&nbsp;&bull; Decreased protein breakdown in the body.</p>\n<p>High urea levels may indicate:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&bull; Excessive dietary protein intake<br>&nbsp;&bull; Increased protein catabolism (e.g., in severe illness, trauma)<br>&nbsp;&bull; Conditions causing increased protein breakdown in the body.</p>",
